{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7865593","formula":"C₁₉H₂₁NO₂","hill":"C19H21NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"H":21.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"URB-602"},"descriptions":{"en":"URB602 ([1,1'-biphenyl]-3-yl-carbamic acid, cyclohexyl ester) is a compound that has been found to inhibit hydrolysis of monoacyl glycerol compounds, such as 2-arachidonoylglycerol (2-AG) and 2-oleoylglycerol (2-OG). It was first described in 2003. A study performed in 2005 found that the compound had specificity for metabolizing 2-AG over anandamide (another cannabinoid ligand) in rat brain presumably by inhibiting the enzyme monoacylglycerol lipase (MAGL), which is the primary metabolic enzyme of 2-AG. However, subsequent studies have shown that URB602 lacks specificity for MAGL inhibition in vitro."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":10979337,"mass":295.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CCC(CC1)OC(=O)NC2=CC=CC(=C2)C3=CC=CC=C3","inchikey":"HHVUFQYJOSFTEH-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"cyclohexyl N-(3-phenylphenyl)carbamate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10979337","atoms":43,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.975,"y":-0.316,"z":1.021,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.374,"y":1.796,"z":0.384,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.808,"y":0.068,"z":0.587,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.3,"y":-0.166,"z":0.522,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.276,"y":-0.169,"z":-1.006,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.186,"y":-1.282,"z":1.073,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.684,"y":-0.108,"z":-1.589,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.593,"y":-1.222,"z":0.49,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.569,"y":-1.222,"z":-1.037,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.066,"y":0.637,"z":0.634,"el":"C"},{"x":0.414,"y":0.685,"z":0.238,"el":"C"},{"x":2.788,"y":0.548,"z":-0.094,"el":"C"},{"x":1.581,"y":-0.062,"z":0.251,"el":"C"},{"x":0.422,"y":2.027,"z":-0.11,"el":"C"},{"x":4.015,"y":-0.219,"z":-0.086,"el":"C"},{"x":2.811,"y":1.897,"z":-0.446,"el":"C"},{"x":1